From: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: disconnect instead of link STA removal

Local patch for ath12k. ath12k returns success for
NL80211_CMD_REMOVE_LINK_STA but keeps the firmware peer of the link
station, because the firmware cannot delete one link of an ML peer.
When hostapd then removes the link (bss.delete() during a reload, the
end of an AP Removal Timer, or an interface removal), the vdev delete of
that link still carries those peers, times out, and both Wi-Fi firmwares
crash.

Every non-AP MLD that holds a link which goes now leaves as a whole,
whichever link it associated on: hostapd frees its entries on every
link without a kernel call each and sends one NL80211_CMD_DEL_STATION
on its association link, so the driver deletes the ML peer on every
link before STOP_AP and REMOVE_LINK run. The delete is sent also when
the driver tears the AP down itself (driver_ap_teardown), since that
teardown removes only the stopped link from the station.

Only bss.delete() and the AP Removal Timer send a Deauthentication
(reason 3) for this. hostapd_free_stas() sends no frame, as for its
other stations, so an interface disable stays silent and the broadcast
DISASSOCIATE, DEAUTHENTICATE and del_client requests keep their own
frame. hostapd_free_stas() replaces the removal of the partner link
stations and the separate pass of hostapd_free_stas_all_links().

The association station is found by the MLD address on the association
link, not by the AID, which another non-AP MLD can hold after the
association station went. Entries left without one are swept on every
link of the AP MLD and deleted once in the kernel, as the earlier
removal of the association station may have skipped its delete; an
entry of a newer association of the same address owns the kernel
station, and then nothing goes to the driver. A session timeout frees
the non-AP MLD on all its links, so it leaves no such entries.
AP-STA-DISCONNECTED is reported once per non-AP MLD: ap_free_sta() of
an association station clears the authorization of its other links.

The AP Removal Timer no longer moves the association of a non-AP MLD
off the removed link, since the move ends with the same link station
removal. A non-AP MLD associated on the link gets the Deauthentication
of hostapd_link_remove_notify_stas() and is freed after its TX status,
before STOP_AP.

Cost: a non-AP MLD reconnects once per removed link. Drivers that can
remove a link station do not need this.

Signed-off-by: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
